# The demo day launch film: 34 MB of video that git cannot delta-compress, in a
# repo that is otherwise ~4 MB. It still reaches production, because deploy.sh
# rsyncs the whole tree and does not consult this file. Master lives in the vault
# at Areas/argo/protocol-camp/final-demo-day/launch-ad/launch-ad-1.mov — see
# scripts/demo-day-pptx/README.md for the encode. The Winston clip next to it is
# small enough to commit, so only this one is listed.
public/demo-day/launch-film.mp4

# The PowerPoint export: 42 MB, and a build artefact rather than a source. Both
# films are embedded inside it, which is the whole point of the file and also why
# it cannot be delta-compressed — every rebuild is 42 MB of new objects in a repo
# that is otherwise ~4 MB.
#
# Regenerate it with `node scripts/demo-day-pptx/build.js`. Do that BEFORE a
# deploy: deploy.sh rsyncs the tree and does not consult this file, so the copy
# on your disk is the copy the site serves. With no copy present the deck's
# download button reads "PPTX not built" rather than breaking, which is the
# intended failure — see PptxLink in src/components/demo-day/Deck.tsx.
public/demo-day/argo-final-demo-day.pptx
